# Deliberately empty of prunes, and the two absences are worth naming so
# neither gets "fixed" back in.
#
# 1. The two externalized Thompson tables (freezeH2O.dat, qr_acr_qg_V4.dat)
#    were excluded here through 2.4.1 because without those lines this
#    sdist exceeded PyPI's 100 MiB per-file cap.  The directory holding
#    them moved to the `gpuwm-data` companion distribution in 2.5.0, so
#    the exclusions moved with it: see gpuwm-data/MANIFEST.in.  There is
#    nothing under gpuwm/ left to exclude.
#
# 2. The top-level `configs/` directory reaches the sdist already:
#    setuptools folds `[tool.setuptools.package-data]` into the source
#    distribution's default file set, so the one declaration that puts the
#    97 repository configs in the wheel puts them in the sdist too
#    (measured, not assumed -- tests/test_configs_are_packaged.py runs
#    sdist._add_defaults_python and counts them).
#    docs/public/VERIFICATION.md's reproduce recipe and docs/public/LES.md
#    both name files under it, so a prune here would make those pages
#    unfollowable from a source build.
#
# tests/test_package_data_coverage.py pins this file against the wheel
# exclusion lists in both pyprojects.

# The companion exclusion is about the OTHER distribution rather than
# about any file's size or license.  `gpuwm-data/` belongs to the
# companion distribution built from `gpuwm-data/pyproject.toml`, and a
# fragment of it inside gpuwm's own artifacts is worse than either whole
# answer: a build carrying `gpuwm_data/__init__.py` and none of its data
# is a package that says where the tables are and has none.
#
# BOTH artifacts leaked it, by two different mechanisms, and this line
# only ever closed one of them:
#
#   sdist -- setuptools' default file set sweeps every .py under the
#     project root, which put `gpuwm-data/gpuwm_data/__init__.py`, and
#     nothing else, inside gpuwm's sdist.  `prune` is the fix and is
#     below.
#   wheel -- [tool.setuptools.packages.find]'s `include` was `gpuwm*`,
#     which is fnmatch over directory names and matched `gpuwm-data`.
#     An earlier version of this comment asserted the opposite -- that
#     `gpuwm-data` is not a valid identifier so no wheel could contain
#     it -- and the built wheel disproved it: a pyproject `find` defaults
#     to `namespaces = true`, and a namespace finder needs no identifier.
#     Fixed where it belongs, in pyproject.toml's `include`/`exclude`,
#     and gated by tests/test_package_data_coverage.py.
prune gpuwm-data

# The staged Rust artifacts are wheel payload, and a SOURCE
# distribution has no business carrying one platform's executables.
# Measured on the 2.5.0 Linux shakeout: `python -m build` after
# `tools/stage_wheel_bridges.py --platform linux-x86_64` swept all 18
# native ELF artifacts in here -- the sdist went from 95,236,252 B to
# 114,906,421 B and shipped Linux binaries as source.  `package-data`
# sweeps the directory into the wheel deliberately (that is the whole
# platform-wheel design) and setuptools folds the same declaration into
# the sdist's default file set, so this is the line that separates the
# two.  setup.py additionally REFUSES an sdist of a staged tree: with
# the prune alone, `python -m build` would build its wheel from the
# pruned sdist and quietly produce a py3-none-any wheel while the
# operator was staging for a platform one.
# tests/test_sdist_excludes_staged_bridges.py measures both halves.
prune gpuwm/libexec/bridges

# Development fault-injection probes are not part of the operational package.
prune tilestream/skeptic

# The pytest suites and the six skeptic_*.py probes that live BESIDE
# tilestream's operational modules.  `prune tilestream/skeptic` above named
# a sub-directory that does not exist, so the 2.7.0 candidate's sdist and
# all three wheels shipped 42 tilestream/test_*.py suites and six probes at
# import top level (measured on the built artifacts).  This line is the
# sdist half; setup.py's build_py filter (DEVELOPMENT_MODULE_GLOBS) is the
# wheel half, and tests/test_operational_package_excludes_probes.py measures
# both.
recursive-exclude tilestream test_*.py skeptic_*.py

# RELEASE-EXCLUDE.txt drops this test with the campaign harness it drives
# (tools/n5s/**) from the public tree, but that manifest governs the
# snapshot builders only and `python -m build` never read it: the 2.7.0
# candidate's sdist carried the test without the harness it imports.  Named
# here so the sdist and the public tree agree; the harness itself is not a
# package in `packages.find` and never reached either artifact.
exclude tests/test_n5s_toolchain.py
# The branch-dispositions gate is development bookkeeping and RELEASE-EXCLUDE.txt
# drops it from the public tree, so the sdist drops it too.
exclude tests/test_branch_dispositions.py
# The three tests c358db8e5 dropped from the public tree with the 2.8.9
# speed-lane bench harness (tools/bench/**) they import; the sdist drops
# them too, or it carries tests without the harness they drive.
exclude tests/test_obs_parallel_native.py
exclude tests/test_regional_packing_bench.py
exclude tests/test_timeline_qualification.py

# The snapshot already excludes these private campaign receipts. Direct
# sdist builds also inherit configs' package-data, so exclude them here too.
exclude configs/da_rerun_286/recent/active-241/case-plan.json
exclude configs/da_rerun_286/recent/active-241/authority/authority-receipt.json
exclude configs/da_rerun_286/recent/large-601-center32p2/case-plan.json
exclude configs/da_rerun_286/recent/large-601-center32p2/authority/authority-receipt.json
exclude configs/da_rerun_286/recent/requested-601-center31/case-plan.json
exclude configs/da_rerun_286/recent/requested-601-center31/authority/authority-receipt.json
exclude configs/da_rerun_286/recent/native-linux-pricing.json
exclude configs/da_rerun_286/recent/native-linux-pricing-241.json

# The README's extracted-source install must have its entry points, and
# its documentation links must resolve in the sdist.  The CHANGELOG's
# links are history: two of its pages (the MCP server guide and the 1.9
# assembly notes) name AI coding agents, which the packet's attribution
# gate refuses in a public asset, so they are read on the repository.
# Include public pages recursively, without sweeping in non-page receipts
# or the internal campaign documents elsewhere under docs/.
include install.sh install.ps1
recursive-include docs/public *.md
# A draft is not documentation: the announcement draft carries the
# project's own attribution text, which the packet's attribution gate
# refuses in a public asset (2.9.2 cut, packet verifier).  It stays
# under docs/public because the claim-backing gate and the resolved-
# scale receipt read it there.
exclude docs/public/ANNOUNCEMENT-DRAFT.md
include docs/public/img/arwen-desktop-2.7.png
include docs/public/receipts/physics-composition-walk.json
include docs/public/receipts/surface-moisture-ledger-accounting.json
include docs/2.7.5-development-record.md docs/2.7.6-development-record.md
include docs/ADAPTIVE-TIMESTEP.md docs/AUTOMATIC-STREAMING-SEARCH.md
include docs/ENSEMBLE_PROVIDERS.md docs/SFIRE-IDEAL.md docs/SFIRE-STATIC.md
include docs/adapt-validation-contract.md docs/arbitrary-verified-adapters.md
include docs/benchmark.md docs/cells.md docs/cumulus-new-tiedtke.md
include docs/da-nowcast-quickstart.md docs/da-vs-wofs.md
include docs/desktop-package-launcher.md
include docs/dev/a65-preparation-peaks.md docs/dev/mynn-gsd41.md docs/dev/verify-exact.md
include docs/ensemble-output-contract.md docs/ensemble-wrf-stochastic-import.md
include docs/gf_gamma_known_delta.md docs/grib2-export.md docs/install.md
include docs/local-da-companion-protocol.md
include docs/migrating-from-wps.md docs/ml-export.md docs/mpas-seam.md
include docs/native_source_adapters.md docs/nowcast-frames.md docs/obs-scorecard.md
include docs/run-output-folders.md docs/run-plan.md
include docs/scoreboard-nightly.md docs/water-temperature-overlay.md
recursive-include docs/manual *.md
recursive-include docs/integration-kit *.md *.json *.py
